// EXPECT: [E086]
// usize -> i64 is a signedness change that loses usize's top half (spec 07: usize is
// [0, 2^N - 1]). It was accepted as a widening until 2026-09-28: the range analysis gives u64 the
// range [0, INT64_MAX] because its domain is i64-based, and read as a bound rather than as
// "unbounded" that made u64 look contained in i64 — so f(2^64 - 1) returned -1.
func f(a usize) i64 {
    var x i64 = a
    return x
}
func main() i32 {
    return 0
}
